<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.4 H3: Enhanced Entity Pages Yield the Strongest Gains ‣ 4 Results ‣ Structured Linked Data as a Memory Layerfor Agent-Orchestrated Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Full pipeline (C6 vs. C1):</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4.4 H3: Enhanced Entity Pages Yield the Strongest Gains ‣ 4 Results ‣ Structured Linked Data as a Memory Layerfor Agent-Orchestrated Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Enhanced+ pipeline (C6+ vs. C1):</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px5" title="In 4.4 H3: Enhanced Entity Pages Yield the Strongest Gains ‣ 4 Results ‣ Structured Linked Data as a Memory Layerfor Agent-Orchestrated Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The agent’s role is complementary, not primary.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS5" title="In 4 Results ‣ Structured Linked Data as a Memory Layerfor Agent-Orchestrated Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.5 </span>Analysis by Query Type</span></a></li>
